{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8231848",
      "title": "Not All Side Effects Need useEffect",
      "sourceHash": "a44784535643e07d490484a6e753a9b3ea810b5183d629844d6ed7593a472b0e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "Now before we dive deeper into useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 6.63,
          "en": "and see more examples for useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.63,
          "end": 9.75,
          "en": "and take a look at the dependencies array again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.75,
          "end": 11.67,
          "en": "I wanna make it very clear that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.67,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "not all side effects require the usage of useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "because overusing useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 24.41,
          "en": "and using it unnecessarily is considered a bad practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 26.4,
          "en": "because you must not forget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.4,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "that this is an extra execution cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "that's triggered after the App component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "or whichever component you're working in execution cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 41.58,
          "en": "So you wanna avoid using useEffect if you don't need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.58,
          "end": 44.49,
          "en": "And here's an example where we don't need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.49,
          "end": 47.73,
          "en": "Let's say here in handleSelectPlace,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.73,
          "end": 50.4,
          "en": "we don't just wanna update the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.4,
          "end": 53.46,
          "en": "to add a place to our list of places here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.46,
          "end": 54.43,
          "en": "when we click on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "but we also wanna store that selected place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 62.13,
          "en": "and the entire list of selected places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.13,
          "end": 65.16,
          "en": "in our browsers storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.16,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "So that when we reload the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "we don't lose these places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "but they're instead still there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 74.103,
          "en": "That's something we might want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.51,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "And to do that we can use another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 81.39,
          "en": "that's built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.39,
          "end": 84.69,
          "en": "We can use the localStorage object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.69,
          "end": 89.69,
          "en": "which just like navigator is provided by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "So localStorage is not coming from React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "not built by me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "is coming from the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 100.71000000000001,
          "en": "And localStorage allows us to use the setItem method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.71000000000001,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "to store some data in the browser's storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "and that data will also be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 108.47999999999999,
          "en": "if we leave the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.47999999999999,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "and come back to it later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 112.38300000000001,
          "en": "or if we reload the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.18,
          "en": "Now, localStorage is relatively easy to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.18,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "You just pass an identifier to setItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "for example, selectedPlaces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 125.58,
          "en": "and then as a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.58,
          "end": 128.43,
          "en": "you pass the value that should be stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.43,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "Though it's important to mention that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 133.713,
          "en": "this data must be in string format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "So you can't store an array or object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 141.96,
          "en": "instead, that data must be converted to a string first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.96,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "which you, for example, can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "with the built in JSON.stringify method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.87,
          "en": "This also is a method and an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.87,
          "end": 153.153,
          "en": "that is provided by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.768,
          "end": 157.65,
          "en": "JSON.stringify for example, takes an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.65,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "and will convert that to a string so that it can be stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 165.9,
          "en": "And the array I wanna pass to JSON.stringify here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.9,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "should be an array of place IDs I selected, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 172.41,
          "en": "So this id which we're getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.41,
          "end": 175.35,
          "en": "and all the previously storedIds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "Therefore, I also need to get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 179.19,
          "en": "all those previously storedIds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.19,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "And we can do that with a localStorage.getItem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "And then of course we have to use the same key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 187.86,
          "en": "as we use for storing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.86,
          "end": 191.17,
          "en": "that will then extract the data from localStorage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.66,
          "end": 196.2,
          "en": "and it will extract it in string format of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 198.63,
          "en": "because that's how the data is stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.63,
          "end": 201.99,
          "en": "So to convert it back to an array, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.99,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "we again have to use the JSON object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 205.95,
          "en": "but now the parse method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.95,
          "end": 209.163,
          "en": "which is basically the opposite of the Stringify method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.32,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "Now of course, we might not have any stored places yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 218.1,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll add some fallback code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "which produces an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 222.753,
          "en": "if this here should yield undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 227.41,
          "en": "And this then gives us our storedIds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.52,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "and we can then use these storedIds here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 235.07999999999998,
          "en": "to spread them into this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.07999999999998,
          "end": 237.15,
          "en": "which we wanna store now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.15,
          "end": 240.12,
          "en": "and add the new Id of the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.12,
          "end": 243.393,
          "en": "that was just selected in front of the storedIds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.86,
          "end": 247.29,
          "en": "So besides updating that data in my state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.29,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "in the currently running application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "which I do in order to update the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "I am also storing this list of IDs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 258.153,
          "en": "in this case in my localStorage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "I also wanna make sure that I don't store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 267.27,
          "en": "an already existing id again in this list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.27,
          "end": 269.13,
          "en": "And therefore, we can add a if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.13,
          "end": 273.787,
          "en": "and check if storedIds already contains this ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.33,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "So this ID I'm getting as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 280.803,
          "en": "we can do that with indexOf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 283.95,
          "en": "And if that yields minus one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.95,
          "end": 287.61,
          "en": "it means this ID is not part of storedIds yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 288.99,
          "en": "and therefore in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 291.24,
          "en": "I want to update the stored data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.24,
          "end": 293.433,
          "en": "Otherwise I don't wanna do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 294.87,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "Now all this code here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 301.27,
          "en": "is just another example for a side effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.34,
          "end": 306.33,
          "en": "because just as fetching the user's location,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.33,
          "end": 309.33,
          "en": "this code down here where we store data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.33,
          "end": 311.28,
          "en": "in the browser's storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 311.28,
          "end": 315.843,
          "en": "is not directly related to rendering this JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 320.1,
          "en": "Updating this state here is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.1,
          "end": 322.29,
          "en": "because those state updates,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.29,
          "end": 326.343,
          "en": "directly lead to a new JSX snapshot in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.57,
          "end": 330.9,
          "en": "But this storage here is totally unrelated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.9,
          "end": 332.94,
          "en": "Still it is of course code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.94,
          "end": 335.07,
          "en": "that's needed in this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.07,
          "end": 338.4,
          "en": "to add this feature where I wanna persist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.4,
          "end": 342.273,
          "en": "this list of places that's created by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.11,
          "end": 345.51,
          "en": "So having this code here is not bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.51,
          "end": 348.06,
          "en": "That's again, really important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 348.06,
          "end": 349.83299999999997,
          "en": "but it is a side effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 351.6,
          "end": 354.54,
          "en": "Now, unlike with the navigator code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.54,
          "end": 357.48,
          "en": "we don't need to wrap this code down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.48,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "with useEffect though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 363.24,
          "en": "And indeed we can't use useEffect here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 363.24,
          "end": 366.03,
          "en": "because we're inside of a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 366.03,
          "end": 369.66,
          "en": "And this usage here would violate the rules of hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 369.66,
          "end": 372.51,
          "en": "because you're not allowed to use React hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.51,
          "end": 374.22,
          "en": "in nested functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 374.22,
          "end": 377.04,
          "en": "if statements or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.04,
          "end": 379.32,
          "en": "They must be used directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.32,
          "end": 382.68,
          "en": "in the root level of your component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 382.68,
          "end": 384.033,
          "en": "like we're using it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 384.87,
          "end": 388.74,
          "en": "But we also don't need useEffect down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.74,
          "end": 392.22,
          "en": "because there's nothing wrong with executing this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.22,
          "end": 395.90999999999997,
          "en": "because this code gets executed when this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.90999999999997,
          "end": 399.18,
          "en": "the handleSelectPlace function is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.18,
          "end": 401.31,
          "en": "which in the end happens when the user clicks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.31,
          "end": 403.11,
          "en": "on one of these items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 403.11,
          "end": 406.62,
          "en": "And then this code does not enter an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 406.62,
          "end": 409.14,
          "en": "because we're not updating any state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 409.14,
          "end": 412.47,
          "en": "And even if we were updating any state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 412.47,
          "end": 416.1,
          "en": "in relation to that localStorage data storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 416.1,
          "end": 417.87,
          "en": "Even if we would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 417.87,
          "end": 420.57,
          "en": "we would not create an infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 420.57,
          "end": 424.23,
          "en": "because again, this code in this handleSelectPlace function",
